<article class="px-4 py-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-12">
    <div class="md:col-span-2">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-base-content">
          About.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-gray-500 mt-2">
          Who's running this thing, and what it is.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="space-y-5">
        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/65 leading-relaxed">
          Hey! I'm Real Limoges. Software engineer on paper; what I
          actually do all day is design machine learning systems.
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/65 leading-relaxed">
          This is where the things I can't stop poking at end up. A lot
          of them turn out to be emergent, a handful of dumb rules run
          enough times until something shows up that nobody put there
          on purpose (a flock, a sandpile avalanche), which I didn't
          plan; it just keeps happening.
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/65 leading-relaxed">
          I think about code like lego, small pieces that snap together
          into something bigger than any of them. The pieces here are a
          little odd: Elixir holding everything together, and C and
          Rust compiled to WASM doing the math right in your browser.
          The fuzzy logic and the mood math used to be Haskell, two
          small libraries (Hazy and Ish) running as their own services
          that the site called over HTTP; they've since been folded
          into the Elixir side. (The bricks on this page build
          themselves up and knock themselves down forever, if you
          wanted a picture of it.)
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/65 leading-relaxed">
          Two things about me show up a lot. I'm colorblind, which is
          how I ended up writing a whole chapter on what color even is.
          And I'm bipolar; the mood journal is me rating my own nights,
          every night for four years, because a doctor told me to.
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/65 leading-relaxed">
          Anyway, it's more fun out here than in a notebook. Poke at
          whatever you like.
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/65 italic mt-8">
          - Real
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="md:col-span-1 flex items-start justify-center md:justify-start md:sticky md:top-24">
      <canvas
        id="lego-stack"
        class="w-full max-w-[320px] aspect-square self-start"
        aria-hidden="true"
      ></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="mt-20">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/85 mb-5">
      What's here
    </h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
      <a
        href="/mood"
        class="group block rounded-lg border-t-2 border-primary bg-base-200 p-6 transition hover:bg-base-300"
      >
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary/70 mb-3">
          Mood
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-base-content mb-2">My mood journal</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50 leading-relaxed">
          Four years of nightly mood ratings (mine), sorted into fuzzy
          states you can scroll through and poke at.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-[11px] text-primary/50 group-hover:text-primary/90 transition">
          explore &rarr;
        </p>
      </a>

      <a
        href="/color"
        class="group block rounded-lg border-t-2 border-accent bg-base-200 p-6 transition hover:bg-base-300"
      >
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent/70 mb-3">
          Color
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-base-content mb-2">A chapter on color</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50 leading-relaxed">
          What color actually is, written by someone who sees less of
          it than you do.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-[11px] text-accent/50 group-hover:text-accent/90 transition">
          explore &rarr;
        </p>
      </a>

      <a
        href="/menagerie"
        class="group block rounded-lg border-t-2 border-secondary bg-base-200 p-6 transition hover:bg-base-300"
      >
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-secondary/70 mb-3">
          Menagerie
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-base-content mb-2">Math playgrounds</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50 leading-relaxed">
          Little sims to break on purpose: flocking birds, sandpiles,
          quantum walks, a fuzzy-logic fan. Every one has sliders.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-[11px] text-secondary/50 group-hover:text-secondary/90 transition">
          explore &rarr;
        </p>
      </a>

      <a
        href="/lab"
        class="group block rounded-lg border-t-2 border-warning bg-base-200 p-6 transition hover:bg-base-300"
      >
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-warning/70 mb-3">
          Lab
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-base-content mb-2">Statistical experiments</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50 leading-relaxed">
          Stats ideas I wanted to see drawn out: what a GAM can do
          that a line can't, and what "Bayesian" actually hands you.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-[11px] text-warning/50 group-hover:text-warning/90 transition">
          explore &rarr;
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-16">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/85 mb-5">
      Elsewhere
    </h2>
    <ul class="text-sm text-base-content/65 leading-relaxed space-y-2">
      <li>
        Code lives on <a
          href="https://github.com/real-limoges"
          class="text-amber-300 hover:text-amber-200 underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-4"
        >
          GitHub
        </a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        This page is one corner of <a
          href="https://realcomplex.systems"
          class="text-amber-300 hover:text-amber-200 underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-4"
        >
          realcomplex.systems
        </a>, which is one Phoenix app doing most things in-process.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-16">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/85 mb-5">
      Colophon
    </h2>
    <p class="font-mono text-xs text-base-content/45 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
      Built with Phoenix and Elixir, LiveView for the interactive bits,
      D3 for the dataviz, and a couple of WASM kernels (C and Rust)
      doing the heavier lifting; those are the lego bricks. There's a <a
        href="/code"
        class="text-amber-300 hover:text-amber-200 underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-4"
      >full parts list</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</article>
